# A stronger exact primary match found in the final high-recall search.
o=byid['1980-519.2']
o['title']='Rational differential operators for a genus-two spectral curve'
o['statement']=r'For a smooth projective genus-two curve over \(\mathbb C\), choose a hyperelliptic model \(w^2=z^5+\beta_4z^4+\cdots+\beta_0\). There exist commuting rational-coefficient ordinary differential operators \(L,M\) whose spectral curve is this model and whose generic common eigenspace has dimension two. The coordinate map is faithful. If instead one insists on every given affine equation \(P\), including a presentation with a nonconstant unit, the analogous ordinary-operator assertion is false; the notebook does not distinguish these readings.'
o['class']='B';o['worth']=''
o['fate']=r'\citet[preprint Thm.~3(2)]{oganesyan2016rational}, first circulated 18 August 2016 and published in 2018, proves the assertion for every quintic coefficient tuple by using the union of two rational-operator families. Thus the abstract genus-two realization question is resolved. Earlier \citet[Thm.~3]{mironov2011selfadjoint} supplies explicit higher-genus families (2011 preprint, online 2013, volume 2014), while \citet[Thm.~1]{davletshinamironov2016orbits} proves the stronger infinite-orbit assertion for generic genus-two curves (2016 preprint, 2017 publication). The chapter’s affine-unit obstruction qualifies the literal prescribed-presentation reading.'
o['present_status']=r'As of November 2026, every smooth projective complex genus-two curve, and every standard monic quintic hyperelliptic model, is realized by rational commuting operators. This is an established result. Universal realization of every affine presentation is false, as the chapter demonstrates using \(zw^2-z^4-1=0\); this distinction is not promoted to an artificial residual open problem.'
o['reconstruction']=r'Commutativity, faithfulness, and the complex base field are supplied. The primary theorem settles the intended abstract-curve or standard-quintic reading; the stronger literal arbitrary-affine-model reading is separated explicitly.'
o['publication_match']='exact';o['refs']=['oganesyan2016rational','mironov2011selfadjoint','davletshinamironov2016orbits']
o=byid['1980-519.3']
o['fate']=r'The Dixmier and Grinevich constructions give genus one; \citet[preprint Thm.~3(2)]{oganesyan2016rational} supplies all complex genus-two curves (2016 preprint, 2018 publication). \citet[Thm.~3]{mironov2011selfadjoint} supplies some hyperelliptic curves of every genus, while \citet[Thm.~1]{davletshinamironov2016orbits} proves an infinite-orbit refinement for generic genus-two curves. These positive subcases do not establish the universal statement for all curves. The chapter proves the field embedding for its displayed family and separates it from affine-coordinate ordinary-operator realizations. The earlier 1977-434.6 is a thematic precursor, without an exact recurring problem ID.'
o['present_status']=r'As of November 2026, all complex curves of genus at most two and explicit higher-genus families have positive realizations. No source proving or disproving the universal curve-function-field conjecture was located in the documented search. This is a search limitation, not a claim that no such theorem exists.'
o['refs']=['dixmier1968weyl','oganesyan2016rational','mironov2011selfadjoint','davletshinamironov2016orbits']
